            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0221" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.00/2–946: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hines</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-09T09:00:00-05:00">February 9, 1946—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:34 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. Department’s circular telegram January 26, 7 p.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">8
                        a.m.</hi>]. In conversation with Foreign Minister<anchor n="49"
                        xml:id="d168-f1"/> yesterday in briefly discussing Argentine matters, I
                    obtained the information which causes me to definitely feel that no approach has
                    been made to Panama on subject of dedication [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >mediation?</hi>]. I am sure Foreign Minister shares view that Argentina
                    holds definite obligation not to one Republic but to all.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hines</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d168-f1" n="49" xml:id="d168-f1-content">
                <p>Ricardo J. Alfaro.</p>
